==========================================================================
4. Hosted model services (not bundled software)
==========================================================================

Alibaba Cloud DashScope (embedding / rerank / chat / vision)

This project calls hosted model APIs over HTTPS. No vendor SDK is involved:
the calls are plain HTTP through Spring's RestClient, so DashScope
contributes no jar, no source and no license obligation to this
distribution. It is disclosed here because using this project may depend on
it and the provider's own terms of service apply independently of this
project's Apache-2.0 license.

Every model capability goes through a port interface in kb-domain
(EmbeddingProvider / RerankProvider / ChatProvider / VisionProvider), and
the embedding, chat and vision paths speak the OpenAI-compatible protocol,
so changing one base URL points them at Azure OpenAI, Ollama, vLLM or any
other compatible endpoint. Leaving the credentials blank is a supported
deployment shape, not a failure: the service starts and runs BM25-only
retrieval.

Note on LangChain4j: the requirements document lists it among candidate
technologies, but this service does **not** depend on it. The model
integrations are hand-written HTTP clients behind the ports above, and no
LangChain4j artifact appears in the build or the packaged jar. It is
recorded here so a future reader does not add a NOTICE entry for a
dependency that is not there.

